  "surprise": "150-fable's exact bigram table re-added at width 384 as 11,449 zero-init rows of 32 dims plus an orthogonal Linear(32, 384) (9,936,416 params as registered). On 153-claude it scored 654/667/682 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 676/700/685: exact means 667.67 vs 687.00, -19.33, paired -22/-33/-3. That is inside the registered -40..+40 but below its central +5. Discard. Pretraining went as predicted: 4405/4282/4420 steps (mean 4369 vs 4503, -3.0%, inside 4,250-4,650, so the table is ~free in steps). Final main val loss was slightly LOWER at 0.0869/0.0833/0.0838 vs 0.0883/0.0869/0.0888, but the minima were mixed (0.0792/0.0786/0.0745 vs 0.0687/0.0778/0.0760), and pretrain held-out greedy fell on 2 of 3 seeds (0.9685/0.945/0.9475 vs 0.9675/0.967/0.968). Surprise: the handed-off model was a much worse sampler, the opposite of 150 at width 256. Round-1 targets solved were 323/375/558 (mean 419) vs 766/747/694 (736), -43%, which falsifies the registered 600-850. Round-1 sample acc was 0.105/0.069/0.132 vs 0.271/0.276/0.212. Whole-run Lean parse failures were 25.9/21.4/19.7% of 266,912 samples vs 15.8/15.5/14.9%, and both-ok samples fell to 307,752 vs 353,098 (-12.8%). This is the same round-1 pathology 148's token batches showed. RL recovered most of it: round-4 solved 1151/1111/1173 (mean 1145 vs 1172; seed 1 below the registered 1,130), with an unchanged eval/round-4 transfer of 0.568/0.600/0.581 vs 0.584/0.599/0.575. The deficit is at lengths 7-9. Deep bins tied or improved: >=10 104/105/110 vs 109/107/107, >=11 26/24/29 vs 26/22/23, >=12 6/4/6 vs 4/5/4, L* 12/11/12 vs 11/12/11. Totals were 1649/1639/1704 s. Untested reading: Adam over-steps rarely hit bigram rows (the sparse-row effect with beta2 0.95), which adds noise to low-count pairs that temperature-0.8 sampling visits. Width, the 32-dim bottleneck and the learned projection are confounded, so this does not say whether 150's full-width table would help at 384 (it cannot fit the cap).",
